      "writtenOn": "2022-11-23T21:59:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`File::from_raw_fd()` will take ownership of the file descriptor, so this is not safe to call if we also keep the `SafeDescriptor` around in the caller. (For example, both `File` and `SafeDescriptor` will try to close the file descriptor when they are dropped.)\n\nIf we really need both alive at once, then the `SafeDescriptor` needs to be cloned first to get a dup\u0027d fd, and then we can use the safe `From\u003cSafeDescriptor\u003e for File` conversion:\n\n```\nlet file: File \u003d vm_descriptor.try_clone().map_err(...)?.into();\n```\n\n(This function would need to be be changed to accept a `SafeDescriptor` or just `File` directly, leaving the caller responsible for the conversion.)",
      "revId": "14cad3abed92984c11468e2096252bb666aa76fa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
